; A rotating run that is infinite.  From (wait) a step stays or wakes, and from
; (wake) it sleeps again.  The run is at (wait) at turns 0, 1 and 3.  At turn 3
; it is back at the configuration of turn 1, (wait) at an odd turn: every
; successor count met, 2 and 1, divides the 2 turns between, so from there it
; wakes and sleeps for ever, a cycle.
(step one)
(observe run)
(schedule rotating)
(wait)
(rule stay (take (wait)) (make (wait)))
(rule wake (take (wait)) (make (wake)))
(rule sleep (take (wake)) (make (wait)))
